scoswm (0.4.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add Debian packaging (debian/) and a quick packaging/build-deb.sh
    so the window manager builds and installs natively on Debian.
  * Harden the SDDM/X11 session entry: TryExec now names the
    scoswm-session entry point, so SDDM only lists SCosWM when the
    session launcher is actually installed and executable.
  * Detect Debian's x-terminal-emulator alternative (and pcmanfm-qt /
    caja / mate-terminal) when choosing the default terminal and file
    manager.
  * Session launcher exports sensible XDG session variables for
    startx/xinit use; under SDDM these are already provided.

 -- Joe <167563398+Joercat@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0400

scoswm (0.4.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Real freedesktop icons for desktop/taskbar/launcher, launcher
    right-click pinning of installed apps to the Home screen, and
    taskbar layout fixes.

